There's an ExecutionOption in XLA called exec_time_optimization_effort which allows to tradeoff compiled binary performance for compilation time.
It would be great if this option could be made available through jax. Maybe something like this.
def f(x):
      return jnp.sqrt(x ** 2) + 1.

f_jit = jit(f)
lowered = f_jit.lower(1.)
lowered.compile( 
    compiler_options={
        "xla_exec_time_optimization_effort": -0.7,
    }
)
